  status: official
  promoted_by: Dave
  promotion_receipt: records/yawn-bot-runtime-promotion-2026-07-11.yawn
  repository_slug_status: current-address

summary: >
  .yawn is an open protocol for inspectable orientation and agency: attributed
  fields, provisional arenas, durable Yawns, causal turns, bounded authority,
  principal-owned objectives, bounded Yawn.bots, proof, and replayable state.

canonical_sentence: >
  .yawn does not contain reality. It makes an agent's orientation toward part
  of reality inspectable, correctable, and replayable.

lexical_invariant:
  product_name: YAWN
  file_extension: .yawn
  contract: core/canonical-extension.yawn
  ingestion_rule: normalize-established-yawn-context-before-creation
  raw_transcript_rule: preserve-when-correction-affects-provenance

protocol_status:
  contracts_v1: stable
  state_substrate_v1: stable
  agency_holarchy_0_2: working-draft
  objective_holon_0_1: working-draft
  orientation_map_0_1: working-draft
  unified_human_document: not-yet-specified

root_loop:
  - signal
  - orientation
  - choice
  - move
  - proof
  - update

constitution: >
  State is the substrate. Desire is attributed directional evidence. Targets
  are optional and scoped. Moves attempt change; proof evaluates results; and
  authorized events rematerialize state.

file_priority:
  - human-readable first
  - machine-addressable second
  - proof-bound when promoted

