boundary:
  - signal is not instruction
  - resonance is not proof
  - coincidence is not command
  - memory is not objective record
  - ai output is not authority
  - intensity is not truth
  - only authorized events update canonical materialized state
  - only suitable evidence or proof upgrades empirical claims
  - desire cannot authorize action
  - confidence cannot ratify an objective
  - objective ratification cannot activate a bot or authorize an effect
  - child bots do not inherit truth consent privacy confidence proof or authority
  - a move cannot mark itself successful
  - transcript normalization cannot change semantic identity or authority
  - presentation preference cannot rewrite orientation semantics or hide a material boundary

first_move:
  instruction: >
    Copy templates/basic.yawn into a new file. Name one thing that has
    attention, record the inference, and do not force the answer.
  proof: "You can point to one clearer next question."
  replay: "What changed after naming it?"

material_record_rule: >
  When an agent or human uses an important file, tool, account, external
  service, backup, GitHub surface, or other access path, record what was used,
  why it mattered, what changed, and what proof or risk remains.

